From aa629b1e47cd87f1cfe55c723d347069ea202413 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Lamb <paul@paulscode.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 20:31:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] onionmsg: carry BOLT 12 messages over onion messages

A new onionmsg package builds blinded paths to this node, sends a
payload to a node id or to a blinded path, and turns delivered onion
messages into typed invoice requests, invoices and invoice errors for
the offers layer. It sits on the upstream onionmessage package, which
relays and delivers the raw messages.

Ported from LND master first, byte for byte: the onion message payload
now carries reply_path as lnwire.BlindedPath, which closes the clash of
two codecs for TLV type 2 in the lnwire package and accepts the sciddir
introduction-node form; and onionmessage gains master's breadth-first
FindPath over nodes that advertise onion messages. The RPC stream and
the route helper follow the type change.

Sending finds a route through the graph whose first hop is a connected
peer, searching from each connected onion peer when the shortest route
starts elsewhere, uses a direct peer when the destination or the
introduction node is one, resolves an introduction node given as a
channel and direction through the channel edge, and processes our own
hop when we are the path's introduction node, the case where the payer
is the miner's only peer. Opening a connection to an unrouted node is
opt-in per send and capped, for fetches this node initiates; a reply to
an inbound message never dials out, since the reply path is the
sender's to choose. Hop data is padded to equal lengths, and the large
onion is used when the payload does not fit the regular one.

Receiving decrypts a copy of our hop's recipient data for the path_id,
decodes the BOLT 12 record, and fans out to registered handlers with a
cap on how many run at once; past the cap messages are dropped rather
than queued. The server's connect hook dials on its own goroutine,
honours the context and waits for the handshake so the new peer's
features are known before it is used.

The offers manager now gets the messenger as its path builder: an offer
minted while the node has a channel peer that speaks onion messages
carries a blinded path through it. The tests route every built onion
through real sphinx routers hop by hop.

(cherry picked from commit a63589d421a21b57a114be5c42fe15e1bb5d2992)
